"epic code" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-code&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-code&gt; element: a folded, highlighted code block in an epic page's prose.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>A folded, highlighted code block in prose. It draws a code-well panel headed by its title, and the code inside, coloured, with a copy button; the code itself is the doc's own <text code>&lt;pre&gt;</>.</>

	<!--
		no <ui-list class="spell-meta">:  its <ui-item>s take Spell UI's "item" style sheet name before the
		              epics pack's elements can, and live examples may draw unstyled (issue I9 of epic-components)
	-->
	<text class="meta" paragraph>For anyone reading or writing an epic page's markup, or changing this element.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its vocabulary (every name it uses): <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-code-epiccode-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-code/EpicCode.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-code/EpicCode.en.ts" code>EpicCode.en.ts</></>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-code-epiccode-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-code/EpicCode.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-code/EpicCode.tsx" code>EpicCode.tsx</></>, with its style sheet (<text code>.css</>) and tests beside it.</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<text paragraph>Two real ones: the first starts open (<text code>open</>, epic <text code>ui-docs-rework</>, J6); the second starts folded (epic <text code>wwod-spell-ui</>, J44).</>
		<html>
			<epic-code title="themes.ts · the new list · 1 line" language="ts" open>
				<pre>static readonly OWN: readonly string\[] = \["spell"]</>
			</>
			<epic-code title="Subclass, markup, form data · 9 lines" language="ts">
				<pre>class UIDoor extends UICheckbox &#123; @E.proto static onValue = "open" @E.proto static offValue = "closed" &#125; // &lt;ui-door name="panel"&gt;Open&lt;/ui-door&gt; chosen:    panel=open unchosen:  panel=closed values:    &#123; panel: "closed" &#125;</>
			</>
		</>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>Live: the real element, drawn by the epics pack this page loads.</>

		<section label="With buttons in its title row" sticky collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>A page's own buttons go in its title row: <text code>&lt;ui-button slot="actions"&gt;</> children (epic <text code>epic-workflow</> P25).</>
			<list bulleted>
				<item>They sit at the right of the title row, after the heading. The heading is its fold button, and it ends where they start.</>
				<item>A click on one never folds or unfolds it.</>
				<item>The docs runtime puts the block's bullhorn there too, so it never sits over a button.</>
				<item>A slotted button's text is never part of the code.</>
			</>
			<example "With buttons in its title row">
				<html>
					<epic-code title="run.sh · 1 line" language="sh">
						<pre>spell run app.spell</pre>
						<ui-button slot="actions" appearance="circular basic" size="mini" icon="play" title="Run it" aria-label="Run it"></ui-button>
					</epic-code>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>From <link title="epics/ui-docs-rework/parts/j6.html" target="src-epics-ui-docs-rework-parts-j6-html" link="/epics/ui-docs-rework/parts/j6.html"><text code>j6.html</></>. The code is text: <text code>&lt;</> for a <text code>&lt;</>.</>
		<text paragraph>j6.html · its code block:</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<epic-code title="themes.ts · the new list · 1 line" language="ts" open>
			  <pre>static readonly OWN: readonly string[] = ["spell"]</pre>
			</epic-code>
			```
		</>
		<text paragraph>145 live ones, in 82 files under <link target="src-epics" link="/epics/"><text code>epics/</></>.</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Where it goes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="map"/>
		<text paragraph>
			<text bold>Its parents:</>
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-list bulleted>
				<ui-item>Anywhere prose goes: it's a <dfn class="spell-term" tabindex="0">prose element</><ui-popup heading="prose element" label="An <epic-*> element marked flow in its vocabulary:  it goes wherever prose goes, so no parent has to list it."></>: <ui-list bulleted><ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-item-html" link="/epic-item"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-item&gt;</></>: among an item's own text, before its cards</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-answer-html" link="/epic-answer"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-answer&gt;</></>, <ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-more-html" link="/epic-more"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-more&gt;</></>, <ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-reply-html" link="/epic-reply"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-reply&gt;</></>: the cards under an item</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-option-html" link="/epic-option"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-option&gt;</></>: an option card's pros and cons</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-field-html" link="/epic-field"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-field&gt;</></>: a phase's field, or a labelled block</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-updated-html" link="/epic-updated"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-updated&gt;</></>: a change to a phase's plan</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-section-html" link="/epic-section"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-section&gt;</></>: an Overview sub-section's prose, or a report's</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-version-html" link="/epic-version"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-version&gt;</></>: an earlier version, kept as it was</> <ui-item>another prose element (a note inside an aside), or plain HTML around it (a <ui-text code>&lt;li&gt;</>, a <ui-text code>&lt;div&gt;</>)</></></>
			</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>
			<text bold>Its children:</>
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>ONE <text code>&lt;pre&gt;</> holding the code as text. A <text code>&lt;pre&gt;</>, so a formatter keeps its white space, and the page shows the code before the pack loads.</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>The <text code>&lt;pre&gt;</> is never shown once the element draws: <text code>&lt;ui-code&gt;</> in its drawing shows the code, so it appears once. It follows its <text code>&lt;pre&gt;</> live: an edit to the file redraws it.</>
	</>

	<section label="4. Attributes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="list check"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Name</>
				<cell>Values</>
				<cell>Meaning</>
				<cell>Required</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>title</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>Its heading: what the code is (<text code>design.ts · 12 lines</>). None: <text code>Code</>.</>
				<cell>no</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>language</>
				</>
				<cell>as <text code>&lt;ui-code language&gt;</> takes it: <text code>ts</>, <text code>html</>, <text code>css</>, <text code>json</>, <text code>spell</>, <text code>text</> for none</>
				<cell>The code's language, for its colours. None: guessed.</>
				<cell>no</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>open</>
				</>
				<cell>present or absent (a boolean)</>
				<cell>Open to start with; a click still folds it, and from then on it's the page's.</>
				<cell>no</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Slots" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<html>
				<ui-text paragraph>A <dfn class="spell-term" tabindex="0">slot</><ui-popup heading="slot" label="Where the element shows its own children:  the doc's prose, inside its drawing."></> is where the element's own children show.</>
			</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Slot</>
					<cell>Holds</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>(default)</>
					<cell>The code: ONE <text code>&lt;pre&gt;</>, its text the code (never drawn itself).</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>actions</>
					</>
					<cell>Buttons of the page's own in its title row (<text code>&lt;ui-button slot="actions"&gt;</>): after the title, before its own buttons; a click on one never folds it. The docs runtime puts the block's bullhorn here too.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Parts" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<html>
				<ui-text paragraph>A <dfn class="spell-term" tabindex="0">part</><ui-popup heading="part" label="A named piece of the element's drawing, which a page's CSS can reach from outside:  epic-note::part(label)."></> is a piece of the drawing a page's CSS can reach.</>
			</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Part</>
					<cell>Is</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>base</>
					</>
					<cell>The panel.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>head</>
					</>
					<cell>Its title row: <text code>toggle</>, then <text code>actions</>.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>toggle</>
					</>
					<cell>Its heading, a <text code>&lt;button&gt;</> that folds it: the chevron, then <text code>heading</>.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>heading</>
					</>
					<cell>The heading's words.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>body</>
					</>
					<cell>What it folds; hidden (<text code>until-found</>) while folded.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>code</>
					</>
					<cell>The <text code>&lt;ui-code&gt;</> that draws the code, highlighted, with its copy button.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>actions</>
					</>
					<cell>In its title row, after the title and before its own buttons: the <text code>actions</> slot.</>
